# The correct pattern for mutually-dependent blocking tasks: SIBLINGS in ONE nursery.
# (Counter-example to examples/parallel_deadlock.chz — see docs/cross-nursery-flat-scheduler.md.)
# Nesting them — an inner `parallel:` or a function that `spawn`s — would deadlock; running one
# inline on the owner would block sequentially. Keep them as siblings at the same level.
fn main():
    a := Channel[int]()
    b := Channel[int]()
    parallel:
        spawn:
            x := a.recv()
            b.send(x)
            print("O got {x}")
        spawn:
            a.send(1)
            y := b.recv()
            print("I got {y}")
    print("done")

main()
